}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Izanami of Eventide''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
One would expect this unit to act just like [[Daybreaker Izanagi (Legend Rare Cat)|Daybreaker Izanagi]], but a key difference is that Izanami of Dusk has '''Area Attack''' rather than Single Target, in addition to having her Insane Damage target Traitless enemies instead. Having some similarities, she keeps some of Izanagi's flaws such as only having 1 standing range against bases, which can allow enemies to kill Izanami easily. Due to this flaw from range mechanics, never use her to try and hit a base, as it will often end in her early demise, as anything can hit her at that point. Also, don't expect an enemy to be hit more than once in a single attack cycle because her multi-hit mostly does not overlap (except at exactly 400 range).

Savage Blow slightly boosts Izanami of Dusk's damage output, as her already pretty high 59,500 (178,500 total with all 3 hits) damage vs Traitless (at level 30) can become an absolutely devastating '''178,500''' damage in a single hit! However, keep in mind that it's only a 20% chance on each hit, so it won't happen often.

It should be noted that while Izanami's damage against Traitless enemies is extremely high, her damage against Traited enemies is very poor, with her average 2.6k DPS at level 30 being below that of even [[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Awakened Mina]]. You should only be using Izanami against Traitless enemies unless you can find an especially good use for her [[Conjure]] ability.

Izanami of Dusk's immunities are also a slight disappointment, as the only truly non-situational immunity is Surge, which gives her notable matchups against [[Master Uril (Enemy)|Master Uril]], [[Kappy Jr.]] and [[Kappy Kawano|his father]], as well as making her useful on stages with a [[Surge Base (Enemy Base)|Surge Base]]. Curse Immunity is mostly irrelevant, as her damage against relic enemies is negligible, though it is still useful in stages with the [[Relic Doge Base (Enemy Base)|Relic Doge Base]] or [[Golem Sunfish]] in stages like [[Ghost King Finale (Brutal)|Ghost King Finale]]. Freeze Immunity helps against [[Henry]], who she can easily snipe with her large attack area.

Izanami of Dusk's Spirit can be extremely useful at times. The knockback and freeze will help in situations such as clearing peons, chipping bosses, and crowd-controlling during difficult situations, all of which can allow your units to press the advantage. Freeze is especially notable for enabling an opportunity for [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]] to get hits in.

Izanami isn't great in stages with few Traitless threats, or when Traitless bosses are supported by many Traited enemies. Even so, one or two annoying Traitless enemies is more than enough justification to bring her if you can afford to do so, as they will quickly make mince meat out of them with little to no objections from their corpses.

