==Trivia==
*Izanami is directly based on [[wikipedia:Izanami|Izanami]] ("She-who-invites" or "Female-who-invites"), one of the primordial central deities of the Japanese creation myth. Together, Izanami and her brother-husband [[Daybreaker Izanagi (Legend Rare Cat)|Izanagi]] are said to have created the islands of Japan and many of the Shinto gods who came to inhabit them, such as [[Shining Amaterasu (Uber Rare Cat)|Amaterasu]], who is considered one of Izanami's "Three Precious Children", and [[Good-Luck Ebisu (Super Rare Cat)|Ebisu]], who is sometimes identified with the twins' misconceived firstborn son Hiruko. The stone floating next to Izanami could represent the ''Yomotsuhirasaka'', the cavern leading to the land of the dead that Izanagi pushed a boulder in front of to separate himself from Izanami after her death.
**Izanami is also the deity of creation and death, as alluded to in her descriptions.

